      "text": "The approach is to take the first block in the file (value-weighted monthly returns), average the three small-cap portfolios and the three big-cap portfolios, and subtract: SMB = mean(SMALL LoBM, ME1 BM2, SMALL HiBM) \u2212 mean(BIG LoBM, ME2 BM2, BIG HiBM). The script treats -99.99 and -999 as missing, skips the rest of the file's sections, and drops any month where SMB cannot be computed. I haven't run it against the full file.\n\n```python\nimport re\nimport numpy as np\nimport pandas as pd\n\nIN_FILE = \"6_Portfolios_2x3.csv\"\nOUT_FILE = \"output.csv\"\nMISSING = {-99.99, -999.0, -999}\n\n\ndef parse_vw_monthly(path):\n    with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"latin-1\") as fh:\n        lines = fh.read().splitlines()\n\n    # Locate the value-weighted monthly block\n    start = 0\n    for i, line in enumerate(lines):\n        if \"Value Weighted Returns -- Monthly\" in line:\n            start = i\n            break\n\n    # Find the header row of that block (contains the portfolio names)\n    hdr = None\n    for j in range(start, len(lines)):\n        if \"SMALL LoBM\" in lines[j]:\n            hdr = j\n            break\n    if hdr is None:\n        for j in range(len(lines)):\n            if \"SMALL LoBM\" in lines[j]:\n                hdr = j\n                break\n    if hdr is None:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"Could not find portfolio header row\")\n\n    rows = []\n    for line in lines[hdr + 1:]:\n        parts = [p.strip() for p in line.split(\",\")]\n        is_data = (\n            len(parts) >= 7\n            and len(parts[0]) == 6\n            and parts[0].isdigit()\n        )\n        if is_data:\n            date = int(parts[0])\n            vals = []\n            for p in parts[1:7]:\n                try:\n                    v = float(p)\n                except ValueError:\n                    v = np.nan\n                if v in MISSING:\n                    v = np.nan\n                vals.append(v)\n            rows.append([date] + vals)\n        elif rows:\n            # End of the monthly VW block (blank line / next section / footer)\n            break\n        # else: skip blank or non-data lines before the first data row\n\n    cols = [\"date\", \"SL\", \"SM\", \"SH\", \"BL\", \"BM\", \"BH\"]\n    df = pd.DataFrame(rows, columns=cols)\n    df[\"date\"] = df[\"date\"].astype(int)\n    return df\n\n\ndef main():\n    df = parse_vw_monthly(IN_FILE)\n\n    small = df[[\"SL\", \"SM\", \"SH\"]].mean(axis=1, skipna=True)\n    big = df[[\"BL\", \"BM\", \"BH\"]].mean(axis=1, skipna=True)\n    smb = small - big\n\n    out = pd.DataFrame({\"date\": df[\"date\"].astype(int), \"value\": smb})\n    out = out.dropna(subset=[\"value\"]).sort_values(\"date\").reset_index(drop=True)\n    out[\"date\"] = out[\"date\"].astype(int)\n    out.to_csv(OUT_FILE, index=False, columns=[\"date\", \"value\"])\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
